Calls: the platform is the guard and R-AP1 (`GET /repos/roc-lang/basic-cli`, `GET /v1/packages/roc-lang/basic-cli/releases`: the GitHub release list of the platform is not read, its route is gone). The start is 0.25.0 (0.26.0 is 1 day old, min-release-age 2 days). The resolve is a free platform and a free nightly: ONE closure query after the compiler download with `groups` [{group of the platform}] (no `range`, no `series`: R-UP3, all series, as registry/al2-upgrade-query run 2), the hash of the start release, and the free compiler window (oldest row to the newest allowed, as registry/cv1-upgrade-free). The answer has the 3 releases and their artifacts (target `x64musl`), no runs, so the ladder is the one of the guard: 4 probes, facts=18 (3 releases x 6 rows). The compiler list is read once and kept (R-IX4, as before).
Queue (R-SH4 detail 12, R-SH3): right after the facts write of the unit probe of the platform: `platform`, `db_query pinned=1`, `clock`, `db_write queue=1` (the baseline, the whole-app check and the app build are not queued: filter 2). After the work (the CI file), the smoke build (R-SM3: sharing on, the key (4oYD, N, x64musl) was built by the ladder, N is installed, no `bot` row, the platform came in the answer and is public): `db_query smoke=1`, `platform`, `db_query pinned=1`, then one `probes` round with `build --target=x64musl main.roc` (as share/sh60-ladder-share), `db_write smoke=1`, then the queue step for the smoke fact, then the send: HA, the unit fact, the smoke fact in one POST. The fake answers 503 (`busy`), so the 3 rows stay (R-SH4: no change of output) and `share.json` is unchanged.
